F DeclareTexturePaintPanels    | TexturePaintSpecification.h | 101   | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing | 🚩 | Declares the workspace's nine panels into the ledger the sequence handed it. nothing about what a layer, a channel or a revision is. at construction. A host that swaps the material ordinal or opens a second document between activations would otherwise present the panels against whatever was standing when the record was first filled. `WorkspaceSpace::DeclarePanelBox` lands every box floating regardless.
    in    Ledger            PanelIndex&  [-]  emptied by the caller before this runs; nine declarations arrive
    in    WorkspaceContext  void*        [-]  a `PaintWorkspaceContext*`; a null context declares nothing at all
    out   -                 void         [-]  ?
    post  the ledger carries one slot per panel, each addressing a context this record owns
    by    Source/TexturePaintSpecification.cpp
